 one  reason why people would go for the  airpods pro but one of the biggest  issues with not having a sealed design  is sound  leakage these ones by far leak the most  amount of sound because they're quite a  bit louder than the airpods too so if  you're going on the bus a lot or out in  public be aware that if you're blasting  music people can probably hear that  around you so if that's a no-no for you  then you might want to avoid the airpods  3. but in general these ones have by far  the best battery life out of the airpods  2 and the airpods pro so it's very very  impressive you're getting about six  hours of battery life compared to five  for the second gen in 4.5  for the airpods pro because they have  the noise cancellation which i'm going  to talk about in just a minute and  that's actually one of the biggest  downsides that you're paying 170  and you're not getting any noise  cancellation however the controls on  these are excellent because all you do  is pinch the stem and it switches the  song pauses does whatever and it's just  super convenient and these also have the  adaptive eq which is very nice and of  course the newer design but in my  personal opinion because the sale is not  that good on these right now  i think you should probably skip out on  these and just go for the airpods pro as  long as they're on sale for this crazy  good price  175 dollars and there are a few reasons  why first of all these airpods pro have  by far  the best in-ear sealed design out of any  in-ear earphones on the market i'm not  kidding because these feature an  exclusive unique vent which basically as  soon as you put them into your ears it  allows some of the air pressure out of  your inner ear canal to release now on  top of that these have by far the  cleanest and tightest base because of  the sealed design compared to the  airpods 3. now another feature that you  can get with the airpods pro the airpods  3 and the airpods max is of course  spatial audio and i think that effect  does such a good job at making it feel  like you're in like an open room with  the sound kind of around you like in a  bigger wider sound stage but by far the  best feature of the airpods pro is the  noise cancellation feature and also the  transparency mode which basically allows  you to listen to music but also hear  your environment and they also do not  leak sound like the other airpods do now  in terms of the actual noise  cancellation performance they do a  really good job and for the average  person you're going to love it because  it blocks out the extra noise and just  allows you to focus and be calm and  peaceful and do your studying work  whatever you want to do without having  to blast your music to drown out that  external noise however the noise  canceling isn't the best because if you  want the best you've got to go with the  air pods max now these are completely  different they're over ear headphones so  they're obviously a lot bulkier i'd say  the airpods max are for those who just  really really want to relax and enjoy  like the best quality music the best  quality speakers being able to hear all  those little instruments that you can't  hear with the other airpods and in terms  of the noise cancellation these are top  notch you can literally put them on and  bring up your music and you won't hear  anything around you literally you won't  hear anything and in terms of the actual  build quality these are by far the best  built headphones that i have ever seen  or experienced it's all metal and the  fabric on the headband is just so soft  and it doesn't put pressure on the top  of your head i love the little digital  crown for adjusting the volume then you  also have the side button for switching  between noise cancellation and  transparency mode which by the way works  excellent on these as well and i know  that spending 450 dollars with the sale  price is a little bit hard to swallow  but if you have the extra cash these are  worth it because you get a totally  different sound quality experience and  these are just such high quality in  terms of the build quality however we do  actually have some leaks and rumors in  terms of which airpods are going to be  updated next now there are a lot of  leaks that later on in 2022 sometime in  the fall we are going to be getting  airpods pro 2 and the biggest feature  that a lot of people are expecting  including myself  is lossless audio support coming to  wireless airpods which right now is not  possible because airpods are using  bluetooth so i think apple is going to  use some kind of different codec  potentially an ultra wide u1 ship so i  think that's coming later on this year  and they might potentially have a  stemless design as well so that's going  to be convenient now in terms of the  airpods max mark german believes that  apple is going to be releasing some new  colors maybe a different case or  something like that and i think they  might be coming at the end of this year  or apple might delay them just so they  don't clash with the airpods pro so  maybe next year we might get new airpods  max and if we do they are for sure also  going to be getting lossless support  which is by far the biggest drawback  right now to the regular airpods max  because they don't support  lossless over wireless which is  unfortunate so with that said hopefully  this video helped you make a decision on  which airpods to buy and if it did go  ahead and click the circle about to  subscribe for more videos like this one  and check out one of those two right  over there thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next video

